      "source": [
        "## 1. Business Case: AirBnb\n",
        "\n",
        "Business problem: Airbnb hosts need a data-informed nightly price. Prices\n",
        "that are too high may reduce bookings, while prices that are too low can limit\n",
        "revenue.\n",
        "\n",
        "Goal: Use NYC listing characteristics, location, availability, and reviews\n",
        "to predict a reasonable nightly listing price.\n",
        "\n",
        "Success measure: Lowest test-set MAE, or average dollar prediction error.\n",
        "Report RMSE and R-squared as supporting measures.\n",
        "\n",
        "How Airbnb could use it: Offer hosts a suggested starting price and a\n",
        "plausible range. It is a pricing aid, not a guarantee of bookings or revenue.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 2. Data Sources and References\n",
        "Primary Dataset: Inside Airbnb Detailed Listings — New York City\n",
        "\n",
        "File used: listings (4).csv.gz\n",
        "- Direct source: Detailed NYC Listings CSV\n",
        "This is the primary dataset for the project. Each row represents one NYC Airbnb listing. It includes the nightly price, borough, neighborhood, room type, property type, capacity, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms, availability, review activity, and ratings. These variables allow us to build models that estimate a competitive nightly price.\n",
        "Supporting Dataset: Inside Airbnb Calendar Data — New York City\n",
        "\n",
        "File used: calendar.csv.gz\n",
        "- Direct source: Detailed NYC Calendar CSV\n",
        "This dataset contains daily availability and minimum/maximum stay rules for listings. The version used does not include daily prices, so it will not be used for seasonal price analysis. Instead, it will be used to measure how often each listing is marked available. Availability does not confirm bookings or demand, but it provides useful background on host behavior.\n",
        "Supporting Dataset: NYC Short-Term Rental Registration Data\n",
        "- Source: NYC Office of Special Enforcement Registration and Listing Data\n",
        "\n",
        "File used: ose-str-registration-dataset-2026-11-02.xlsx\n",
        "\n",
        "*   This official NYC dataset contains short-term rental registration information and associated listing IDs. It will be used as a supporting descriptive analysis to identify whether an Airbnb listing ID appears in the registration data. A match provides regulatory context, while a non-match does not automatically mean a listing is operating illegally because the datasets may differ by date, format, or platform status.\n",
        "Business Context References\n"
      ],
